rd whichever celestial body exerts the stronger pull, creating high tide, while the opposite side of the planet also experiences a bulge due to inertia, producing a second high tide. Most coastlines experience two high and two low tides roughly every 24 hours and 50 minutes, though some regions have a single daily cycle or irregular patterns shaped by local geography. When the Sun and Moon align during new and full moons, their combined pull produces spring tides, which have greater range. When they sit at right angles during the first and third quarter phases, the forces partly cancel, producing neap tides with smaller variation. Tides shape ecosystems, influence navigation and fishing, and drive tidal energy projects. Their timing can be predicted with great accuracy, which makes them among the most reliably forecast phenomena in nature.", "ttft_ms": 2570, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 2635, "uuid": "8567aefb-a312-456b-9b4e-048ee9fac883", "begun_message_ids": ["msg_011ChTf57KCecjdvJ1N68e2w"], "ttft_stream_ms": 864, "time_to_request_ms": 104, "first_content_frame_ms": 868, "user_message_uuid": "18f0856d-8166-440a-a082-80b8627e048c", "user_message_uuids": ["18f0856d-8166-440a-a082-80b8627e048c"], "request_sent_wall_ms": 1795792742372, "first_request_input_tokens": 21032, "first_request_cache_read_input_tokens": 13387, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "model_usage_since_last_result": {"claude-haiku-5-5": {"inputTokens": 2, "outputTokens": 331, "cacheReadInputTokens": 13387, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 7643, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.00182817, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens": 7643, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "credential_expires_at": "2026-12-02T08:59:25.377Z"}
